+
+### 5.1 Token quick fields (UX-07 / UI-TOKEN-01 data)
+
+Before M7 character sheets, quick values come from `Entity.token.quickFields`, never a character-sheet lookup or invented defaults. Field IDs are lowercase registry keys (1–32 characters, letters/digits/underscore/hyphen, starting with a letter; prototype keys excluded), with at most 32 fields per token. Values are finite numbers; optional colours use `#rrggbb`. Default preview IDs are `hp`, `ac`, `speed`. Speed is stored in grid cells and displayed using the current scene's `unitsPerCell` and `unitLabel`. Other values are system-neutral numbers.
+
+Each field has its own `visibility`: `all` for viewers of the entity, `owner` for host/co-DM/owning seats, or `dm` for host/co-DM. Entity/layer/view-permission gates still apply. The game host removes the entire field (value, colour and policy) before serializing snapshots or patches to other audiences. The client resolver maps absent entries to **not shared**; unset and private entries are intentionally indistinguishable. Ownership, seat-role and permission changes recompute the view.
+
+`token.setQuickField { sceneId, entityId, fieldId, field }` is a durable action, with `field: null` removing a field. Normal edit permissions and layer locks apply. Admins on that layer may initialize fields and change sharing/colours; other editors may update an existing visible value while retaining its policy/colour. Mods and spectators cannot submit it. `entity.create` may seed fields; `entity.update` preserves them when replacing a token component and accepts only unchanged visible field echoes. Thus an editor cannot erase or overwrite values absent from their filtered view.
+
+The three ordered registry IDs are a browser-local per-viewer preference, stored under `mythic.quick-fields.v1:<encoded identityId>` (no secret). The client `loadQuickFieldSelection` / `saveQuickFieldSelection` API validates exactly three distinct IDs and defaults to HP/AC/Speed on missing or corrupt storage. These are presentation preferences, not campaign state or actions. Registry extensions can supply other IDs. UX-19 consumes `quickFieldPreview` and supplies the scene grid; its card and preference controls remain separate UI work.
+
+Save schema **v3** adds this optional component; the v2-to-v3 migration preserves old data without fabricating values, including nested snapshot versions. Golden fixtures retain v1/v2 and add v3. Protocol **v3** requires matching clients so older clients cannot silently discard quick fields. Action envelopes and coordinates are unchanged.
 
